69
00:04:52,588 --> 00:04:54,018
Hey, call her over.

70
00:04:55,458 --> 00:04:56,888
What, time to check out her body?

71
00:04:57,558 --> 00:04:59,658
- Want to make a bet? - What is it?

72
00:04:59,658 --> 00:05:03,998
- Whoever's closest, meal is free. - Deal.

73
00:05:04,228 --> 00:05:05,238
Go ahead, call her.

74
00:05:05,798 --> 00:05:09,368
I'm guessing a full B-cup.

75
00:05:09,568 --> 00:05:13,908
- No. - No, you idiot. I say 75B.

76
00:05:13,978 --> 00:05:16,448
- No way. There's nothing there. - Darn, did you touch them?

77
00:05:16,578 --> 00:05:18,348
I said no. It's 75B.

78
00:05:18,408 --> 00:05:21,818
- Do you guys not know your ABCs? - You guys are...

79
00:05:24,218 --> 00:05:25,258
Darn it.

80
00:05:26,958 --> 00:05:28,858
Is this jerk crazy?

81
00:05:40,238 --> 00:05:42,638
- Hey, look at this. Darn it. - I'm sorry.

82
00:05:42,708 --> 00:05:44,908
Hey, look at me. Look at this guy, he's speechless.

83
00:05:44,968 --> 00:05:48,578
That's it. Forget it. We're not settling this.

84
00:05:48,778 --> 00:05:51,108
His uncle is a big shot at the prosecutor's office.

85
00:05:51,578 --> 00:05:53,978
Call him and have this jerk arrested and thrown in jail.

86
00:05:54,048 --> 00:05:55,048
Yes, that's right.

87
00:05:55,118 --> 00:05:58,888
Hey, call The Bear from Mapo, Bulldog from Yongsan,

88
00:05:59,088 --> 00:06:00,388
and The Viper from Wangsimni.

89
00:06:00,458 --> 00:06:02,558
Tell them to come teach this jerk a lesson.

90
00:06:02,628 --> 00:06:04,228
Should I?

91
00:06:04,228 --> 00:06:06,698
You want me to completely ruin this jerk's life?

92
00:06:06,758 --> 00:06:10,598
Yes, call them. Call them all. The prosecutors, the police,

93
00:06:10,668 --> 00:06:13,298
the Bear, the Bulldog, the Viper. Call every animal you know.

94
00:06:13,438 --> 00:06:14,438
You had better call them.

95
00:06:14,498 --> 00:06:16,008
Or I'll throw all of you in a zoo cage...

96
00:06:16,068 --> 00:06:18,008
- and lock you up. - Wait, Kim Mu Jin.

97
00:06:19,708 --> 00:06:21,538
I have no intention of settling with jerks like you,

98
00:06:21,608 --> 00:06:23,008
so let's take this outside. What do you say?

99
00:06:23,078 --> 00:06:26,418
Who's first? Want to go one-on-one? Or all at once?

100
00:06:26,478 --> 00:06:27,778
I'm good either way, so let's fight.

101
00:06:27,848 --> 00:06:29,188
I'll pay for all your hospital bills,

102
00:06:29,248 --> 00:06:31,518
so come on out. Let's fight. Get out here!

103
00:06:31,518 --> 00:06:33,058
I'll take all of you on. I mean it.

104
00:06:33,058 --> 00:06:36,658
- Get out here now. - Hey, just try it.

105
00:07:34,718 --> 00:07:37,188
I know the customer was being a total jerk,

106
00:07:37,948 --> 00:07:39,418
but the customer is always right.

107
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:42,058
Are you out of your mind hitting a customer?

108
00:07:45,158 --> 00:07:47,598
That's what the Manager said to me.

109
00:07:48,998 --> 00:07:51,698
So I told her I'd report it to the police myself.

110
00:07:52,268 --> 00:07:53,568
As the victim.

111
00:07:55,068 --> 00:07:56,768
And I said I'd file a complaint against her...

112
00:07:56,838 --> 00:07:58,908
with the company for failing to protect an employee.

113
00:08:03,148 --> 00:08:07,178
Well, the Manager's face went pale, of course. And those jerks...

114
00:08:07,248 --> 00:08:08,788
ran off without a second glance.

115
00:08:14,188 --> 00:08:15,688
I'm not made of steel.

116
00:08:18,428 --> 00:08:19,898
And I'm not a rock.

117
00:08:23,198 --> 00:08:24,698
When someone stands up for me,

118
00:08:25,998 --> 00:08:27,238
is kind to me,

119
00:08:28,738 --> 00:08:31,068
and cares about me, my heart is swayed too.

120
00:08:32,978 --> 00:08:34,438
I'm only human.

121
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:38,878
What is that...

122
00:08:40,218 --> 00:08:41,378
supposed to mean?

123
00:08:44,918 --> 00:08:45,918
I am...

124
00:08:48,358 --> 00:08:51,628
telling you that I'm developing feelings for you, Mu Jin.

125
00:09:00,638 --> 00:09:01,638
So does that mean we're...

126
00:09:03,708 --> 00:09:04,708
going out now?

127
00:09:10,548 --> 00:09:12,648
I go to bed at midnight and wake up at 4am.

128
00:09:12,718 --> 00:09:15,018
I deliver health drinks for three and a half hours,

129
00:09:15,988 --> 00:09:17,788
and as soon as I get home, I wake up my siblings...

130
00:09:17,848 --> 00:09:19,018
and get them ready for school.

131
00:09:19,088 --> 00:09:23,158
After I feed them and send them off, I do the dishes and the laundry,

132
00:09:23,228 --> 00:09:25,088
vacuum the house, and mop the floors.

133
00:09:25,458 --> 00:09:28,058
Then I go straight to a six-hour part-time job, and when that's over,

134
00:09:28,228 --> 00:09:30,798
I go right to the next part-time job for five hours.

135
00:09:30,798 --> 00:09:34,168
When I get home after all that, I clean up the house and wash up,

136
00:09:35,038 --> 00:09:38,208
and then I pass out. The next day, I have to wake up at 4am again.

137
00:09:40,308 --> 00:09:43,648
Out of 24 hours, I don't even have an hour to live for myself,

138
00:09:44,478 --> 00:09:46,348
and there's no room for you to squeeze in.

139
00:09:47,878 --> 00:09:50,518
So don't sway my heart anymore.

140
00:09:51,448 --> 00:09:52,988
Don't be kind to me,

141
00:09:53,658 --> 00:09:54,918
don't be warm to me,

142
00:09:55,688 --> 00:09:57,888
and don't get angry on my behalf like this.

143
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:01,458
Just nothing more and nothing less.

144
00:10:03,868 --> 00:10:05,368
Please treat me as just a coworker.

145
00:10:36,828 --> 00:10:39,338
Bravo.

146
00:10:39,498 --> 00:10:42,438
Excellent. He gave them a good scolding.

147
00:10:42,538 --> 00:10:44,868
We can't let guys like those even set foot in there.

148
00:10:45,408 --> 00:10:47,578
Secretary Cha. I'm not just saying this...

149
00:10:47,638 --> 00:10:48,638
because he's my son.

150
00:10:48,778 --> 00:10:52,278
- Isn't Mu Jin cool and wonderful? - Yes, he certainly is.

151
00:10:53,718 --> 00:10:56,618
I didn't realise Mu Jin was the type...

152
00:10:56,688 --> 00:10:59,458
to go that far in the name of justice.

153
00:11:01,388 --> 00:11:04,828
When it's later revealed that Mu Jin is my son,

154
00:11:04,888 --> 00:11:07,058
this will be a big help to his image, won't it?

155
00:11:07,128 --> 00:11:08,898
Yes, I believe it will.

156
00:11:09,898 --> 00:11:12,868
I won't praise or scold Mu Jin for what happened today.

157
00:11:12,938 --> 00:11:15,168
Act as if I was never briefed on this.

158
00:11:15,168 --> 00:11:18,368
- I don't know anything about it. - Understood. Well, then.

159
00:11:18,838 --> 00:11:20,078
Don't tell me...

160
00:11:21,308 --> 00:11:23,808
Mu Jin and that part-timer...

161
00:11:23,878 --> 00:11:27,318
- who was harassed are involved. - Kim Yoon Jin.

162
00:11:30,088 --> 00:11:31,518
What?

163
00:11:32,488 --> 00:11:34,358
You look like I have hit a nerve.

164
00:11:36,188 --> 00:11:39,198
Are Mu Jin and that part-timer really dating?

165
00:11:40,228 --> 00:11:41,658
I will look into it.

166
00:11:42,228 --> 00:11:43,468
No, I mean...

167
00:11:44,368 --> 00:11:46,738
If you know something, just tell me the truth.

168
00:11:49,168 --> 00:11:51,708
The Manager has her suspicions as well,

169
00:11:52,308 --> 00:11:55,208
but I will investigate promptly and give you an accurate report.

170
00:11:59,678 --> 00:12:01,248
Interesting.

171
00:12:02,018 --> 00:12:04,188
That part-timer must be something else.

172
00:12:05,218 --> 00:12:07,288
Mu Jin has only been working there for a few days.

173
00:12:09,028 --> 00:12:11,058
How did she manage to sway his heart so quickly?

174
00:12:14,228 --> 00:12:16,098
He's dating a part-timer?

175
00:12:17,628 --> 00:12:19,938
That arrogant kid?

176
00:12:50,498 --> 00:12:52,228
It's too late. You should go.

177
00:13:04,378 --> 00:13:05,948
Han Gyu Min, Han Gyu Seo.

178
00:13:06,648 --> 00:13:07,918
Han Gyu Min, Han Gyu Seo, wake up.

179
00:13:08,518 --> 00:13:10,018
You have to brush your teeth...

180
00:13:10,088 --> 00:13:12,218
and wash your faces before bed. Get up.

181
00:13:12,558 --> 00:13:15,928
Hurry. Get up.

182
00:13:16,358 --> 00:13:17,358
Go wash up.

183
00:13:22,498 --> 00:13:24,598
Do not just rush through it. Brush up and down,

184
00:13:24,668 --> 00:13:27,568
and get every corner, you hear? I'm going to check later.

185
00:13:41,518 --> 00:13:42,918
(There was not a single thing to eat in the fridge.)

186
00:13:45,318 --> 00:13:48,518
There was not a single thing to eat in the fridge.

187
00:13:49,188 --> 00:13:50,928
Next time, you should at least make...

188
00:13:50,988 --> 00:13:52,958
the tuna kimchi stew your father likes.

189
00:13:53,598 --> 00:13:55,828
Be a good daughter. That is how you will be blessed.

190
00:13:56,298 --> 00:13:57,298
Your father.

191
00:14:09,208 --> 00:14:10,378
Gyu Rim!

192
00:14:11,178 --> 00:14:14,678
I brushed my teeth, washed my face, and put on lotion.

193
00:14:14,848 --> 00:14:18,018
Really? Let me see. Open your mouth.

194
00:14:18,348 --> 00:14:20,118
So clean.

195
00:14:20,518 --> 00:14:22,018
- Gyu Seo, time for bed. Lie down. - Okay.

196
00:14:28,398 --> 00:14:29,528
- Sleep well, Gyu Seo. - Okay.

197
00:14:29,598 --> 00:14:31,328
- Sweet dreams. - Okay.

198
00:14:43,208 --> 00:14:44,708
Han Gyu Oh, where are you?

199
00:14:45,848 --> 00:14:48,418
I am going to wait up for you,

200
00:14:48,918 --> 00:14:50,118
so come home and talk to me.

201
00:15:02,798 --> 00:15:05,468
The guy who only used to drink expensive wine and whiskey...

202
00:15:06,198 --> 00:15:09,308
is now drinking beer at a convenience store.

203
00:15:10,068 --> 00:15:12,738
Are you enjoying slumming it these days?

204
00:15:13,778 --> 00:15:15,308
I confessed to Han Gyu Rim.

205
00:15:18,508 --> 00:15:19,918
What? Which Han Gyu Rim?

206
00:15:21,478 --> 00:15:23,748
Do not tell me it is the Han Gyu Rim who gave me the packed lunch.

207
00:15:24,388 --> 00:15:25,388
The one I asked you to set me up with,

208
00:15:25,448 --> 00:15:28,188
for the first time in my life, and you completely ignored me. Her?

209
00:15:31,758 --> 00:15:34,728
So... I see.

210
00:15:35,258 --> 00:15:36,328
Unbelievable.

211
00:15:38,398 --> 00:15:39,738
What happened?

212
00:15:45,608 --> 00:15:46,638
I got rejected.

213
00:15:55,348 --> 00:15:56,348
Hey.

214
00:15:56,618 --> 00:15:58,318
This is the best thing I have heard all year.

215
00:15:58,318 --> 00:16:00,218
It is hilarious. Serves you right.

216
00:16:02,458 --> 00:16:04,588
Sure, laugh it up.

217
00:16:11,898 --> 00:16:12,968
Why did she reject you?

218
00:16:14,968 --> 00:16:16,038
She said it did not feel right.

219
00:16:17,838 --> 00:16:19,038
What does not?

220
00:16:21,038 --> 00:16:24,848
Then again, when a guy is too handsome like you,

221
00:16:25,008 --> 00:16:26,978
women find it burdensome and do not like it.

222
00:16:27,048 --> 00:16:28,548
It just makes them feel insecure.

223
00:16:28,748 --> 00:16:32,318
Someone like me, who is just average and pleasantly handsome,

224
00:16:32,618 --> 00:16:34,518
is comfortable, reassuring, and just right.

225
00:16:36,758 --> 00:16:37,858
No.

226
00:16:38,628 --> 00:16:39,658
She said...

227
00:16:40,658 --> 00:16:44,268
she does not have the luxury of dating or liking anyone.

228
00:16:45,328 --> 00:16:47,638
How can you be too busy to date someone?

229
00:16:47,838 --> 00:16:49,038
Should I just tell her I am well-off?

230
00:16:49,098 --> 00:16:50,768
No, should I just reveal everything...

231
00:16:50,838 --> 00:16:52,838
and say I am actually from a rich family?

232
00:16:54,308 --> 00:16:56,978
And that I will give her the very luxury she says she lacks.

233
00:16:58,408 --> 00:17:00,018
That she shouldn't worry and just leave it to me.

234
00:17:00,078 --> 00:17:02,348
Are you out of your mind?

235
00:17:02,348 --> 00:17:04,688
- That's cheating. - What is?

236
00:17:04,748 --> 00:17:07,018
Even I'm not going to tell her about my dad's abalone farm.

237
00:17:08,588 --> 00:17:10,858
To be blunt, it's not even yours. Right?

238
00:17:11,388 --> 00:17:13,328
You haven't properly inherited it yet.

239
00:17:16,628 --> 00:17:17,628
That's true.

240
00:17:19,738 --> 00:17:20,898
But her telling me...

241
00:17:22,468 --> 00:17:24,508
not to mess with her feelings...

242
00:17:24,538 --> 00:17:25,978
and not to think about her...

243
00:17:26,938 --> 00:17:28,038
She must want me to pay more attention...

244
00:17:28,108 --> 00:17:30,578
and pursue her. Why do I keep hearing it like that?

245
00:17:30,678 --> 00:17:34,518
That's just you hearing what you want to hear. Okay?

246
00:17:36,088 --> 00:17:38,118
Like Gyu Rim said, don't mess with her.

247
00:17:38,918 --> 00:17:40,158
Especially when you can't take responsibility.

248
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:42,688
Why can't I be responsible for her?

249
00:17:43,328 --> 00:17:45,158
Why are you suddenly yelling?

250
00:17:45,428 --> 00:17:48,928
- Why? Got caught having fun? - What?

251
00:17:49,468 --> 00:17:51,198
What about you? Did you ask me to introduce you...

252
00:17:51,268 --> 00:17:54,468
so you could have a little fun? Aren't you crazy?

253
00:17:54,468 --> 00:17:55,938
What are you talking about? Am I you?

254
00:17:55,938 --> 00:17:58,408
- Do you think we're the same? - You and I are different.

255
00:17:59,008 --> 00:18:01,108
I'm more handsome than you, have more money,

256
00:18:01,208 --> 00:18:03,008
I'm smarter, and I have more hair.

257
00:18:03,008 --> 00:18:05,548
Don't you see that all that is your baggage?

258
00:18:05,608 --> 00:18:07,218
It's what keeps people away.

259
00:18:08,278 --> 00:18:12,688
I'm not the eldest son like you. I'm not from a rich family like you,

260
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,688
so I don't have a position or a company to inherit.

261
00:18:15,118 --> 00:18:16,158
And my mom...

262
00:18:16,858 --> 00:18:18,788
says as long as I bring a woman home,

263
00:18:18,858 --> 00:18:21,928
she'll accept anyone. But your mom isn't like that.

264
00:18:23,968 --> 00:18:25,698
Hey, let's be honest.

265
00:18:25,698 --> 00:18:27,598
The Chairman will ask about her parents,

266
00:18:27,768 --> 00:18:30,068
what school she went to, what her job is,

267
00:18:30,068 --> 00:18:31,808
and what her siblings do.

268
00:18:32,038 --> 00:18:34,038
Isn't it natural for her to weigh all those things?

269
00:18:34,108 --> 00:18:35,108
You don't get that?

270
00:18:39,818 --> 00:18:40,818
You're right.

271
00:18:42,318 --> 00:18:44,488
You're exactly right.

272
00:18:45,588 --> 00:18:47,018
Thanks. You told me the right thing.

273
00:18:47,088 --> 00:18:48,788
When have I ever been wrong? I told you the right thing.

274
00:18:52,158 --> 00:18:54,228
That jerk. When he has nothing left to say,

275
00:18:54,298 --> 00:18:55,298
he just hits people.

276
00:18:55,698 --> 00:18:58,198
It was a strange place where the sign...

277
00:18:58,268 --> 00:19:00,298
made of chocolate was melting.

278
00:19:05,108 --> 00:19:08,578
Hey, I know you're clueless, but how can you not read English?

279
00:19:08,678 --> 00:19:10,878
Dry clean only. Do you not know what "dry clean only" means?

280
00:19:15,178 --> 00:19:16,448
Only dry clean.

281
00:19:16,548 --> 00:19:19,118
Even a first-grader knows that. Are you a birdbrain?

282
00:19:19,458 --> 00:19:21,358
Did I tell you to get this dry-cleaned or not?

283
00:19:21,658 --> 00:19:23,558
How could you just throw this in the washing machine?

284
00:19:23,628 --> 00:19:24,788
Do you know how much this costs?

285
00:19:25,528 --> 00:19:28,398
I'm sorry. I was distracted and didn't see it.

286
00:19:29,028 --> 00:19:30,098
Is it very expensive?

287
00:19:30,468 --> 00:19:31,728
It costs more than what you make in a month...

288
00:19:31,798 --> 00:19:32,898
at your part-time job. Happy now?

289
00:19:34,198 --> 00:19:37,238
Gyu Min, let's go to bed. I'll read the rest tomorrow.

290
00:19:37,508 --> 00:19:38,508
Good night.

291
00:19:39,538 --> 00:19:41,738
How are you going to pay for this?

292
00:19:44,578 --> 00:19:46,678
The kid needs to sleep, so stop being loud and come out.

293
00:19:52,188 --> 00:19:53,358
Unbelievable.

294
00:19:56,088 --> 00:19:57,758
You ruined it, so you're paying for it.

295
00:19:58,258 --> 00:20:01,598
Either wire me 1,500 dollars now or make it like new again.

296
00:20:02,528 --> 00:20:04,398
How can one blouse be that expensive?

297
00:20:05,168 --> 00:20:07,468
Where in the world is there a 1,500-dollar blouse?

298
00:20:07,538 --> 00:20:11,938
Right here. It might not exist in your world, but it does in mine.

299
00:20:12,108 --> 00:20:13,808
How are you going to pay for this?

300
00:20:15,008 --> 00:20:17,478
I don't have that kind of money. I can't pay for it.

301
00:20:20,548 --> 00:20:22,678
Instead, you can take anything you want from my clothes.

302
00:20:25,088 --> 00:20:26,388
Why would I wear your clothes?

303
00:20:26,918 --> 00:20:28,788
How could I possibly wear those rags?

304
00:20:30,988 --> 00:20:32,898
Well, this wouldn't have happened...

305
00:20:32,958 --> 00:20:35,028
if you had just taken care of the blouse yourself.

306
00:20:41,498 --> 00:20:42,498
Han Gyu Young.

307
00:20:43,868 --> 00:20:44,868
What?

308
00:20:46,238 --> 00:20:47,808
I'm curious about something.

309
00:20:48,778 --> 00:20:50,448
Why do you live the way you do,

310
00:20:51,108 --> 00:20:53,678
and why do I live the way I do?

311
00:20:55,478 --> 00:20:56,488
What are you talking about?

312
00:20:57,548 --> 00:20:59,918
You get to do everything you want,

313
00:21:00,418 --> 00:21:01,418
but why can't I...

314
00:21:03,058 --> 00:21:05,158
do a single thing I want to do?

315
00:21:07,558 --> 00:21:08,728
Because you're the eldest daughter.

316
00:21:08,898 --> 00:21:10,628
The eldest daughter who's only a year older than you?

317
00:21:11,428 --> 00:21:12,698
Besides, since you were born early in the year,

318
00:21:13,038 --> 00:21:15,368
we were in the same grade since elementary school.

319
00:21:16,098 --> 00:21:19,268
You're the nice one. You're always giving and selfless,

320
00:21:19,338 --> 00:21:20,608
and so compassionate, an eldest daughter trait.

321
00:21:21,608 --> 00:21:22,638
Then...

322
00:21:23,678 --> 00:21:26,008
what would happen if I started living like you?

323
00:21:26,478 --> 00:21:27,778
What are you going on about now?

324
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:30,648
Like Gyu Min says, you're Kongjwi, and I'm Patjwi.

325
00:21:31,118 --> 00:21:33,058
We're just playing our parts.

326
00:21:33,558 --> 00:21:35,418
It's in your DNA. You were born that way.

327
00:21:36,188 --> 00:21:37,988
No one's just born that way.

328
00:21:38,788 --> 00:21:39,958
It's because you won't do it.

329
00:21:40,728 --> 00:21:42,498
Because there's no one else to do it but me.

330
00:21:43,098 --> 00:21:45,898
Because if I didn't do it either, the whole house would be a mess.

331
00:21:46,868 --> 00:21:47,998
I do it because I have to.

332
00:21:49,268 --> 00:21:50,708
And I'm not nice.

333
00:21:51,408 --> 00:21:52,708
I'm selfish too.

334
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:56,808
I want to wear nice things and eat good food too.

335
00:21:57,308 --> 00:22:01,048
I want to study, and I want to hang out with my friends too.

336
00:22:01,048 --> 00:22:02,218
I also want a good person...

337
00:22:05,148 --> 00:22:06,148
All right.

338
00:22:06,218 --> 00:22:08,088
You don't have to pay me back for the blouse.

339
00:22:09,388 --> 00:22:10,388
Are we good?

340
00:22:11,258 --> 00:22:12,258
Everyone, watch out.

341
00:22:12,328 --> 00:22:14,598
Bruce Banner is about to turn into the Hulk.

342
00:22:34,748 --> 00:22:35,778
What about my mom?

343
00:22:36,448 --> 00:22:39,488
She says to bring home any woman, and she'll accept her.

344
00:22:39,558 --> 00:22:41,688
But your mom isn't like that.

345
00:22:41,958 --> 00:22:42,958
Hey, let's be honest.

346
00:22:42,958 --> 00:22:44,958
The Chairman will ask about her parents,

347
00:22:44,958 --> 00:22:47,228
what school she went to, what her job is,

348
00:22:47,228 --> 00:22:48,998
and what her siblings do.

349
00:22:49,228 --> 00:22:51,028
Isn't it natural for her to weigh all those things?

350
00:22:51,098 --> 00:22:52,298
You don't get that?

351
00:23:05,648 --> 00:23:06,678
Come in.

352
00:23:10,248 --> 00:23:11,488
You're still up?

353
00:23:12,518 --> 00:23:13,658
I can't sleep.

354
00:23:14,788 --> 00:23:17,228
Why not? Aren't you tired?

355
00:23:19,128 --> 00:23:20,528
There's a woman I like.

356
00:23:22,928 --> 00:23:24,098
Oh, really?

357
00:23:25,128 --> 00:23:26,128
But...

358
00:23:26,768 --> 00:23:29,168
I told her how I feel, and she turned me down.

359
00:23:31,738 --> 00:23:35,808
Goodness. What kind of amazing woman would dare turn down our Mu Jin?

360
00:23:36,808 --> 00:23:37,808
But...

361
00:23:38,878 --> 00:23:40,418
I'm not going to give up on her.

362
00:23:41,278 --> 00:23:42,378
But you said she turned you down.

363
00:23:42,988 --> 00:23:45,888
That may be her decision, but I'm not giving up.

364
00:23:47,018 --> 00:23:48,018
I see.

365
00:23:48,318 --> 00:23:51,228
Well, that's a good attitude to have.

366
00:23:53,428 --> 00:23:55,058
But do you realise this is the first time...

367
00:23:55,128 --> 00:23:56,498
you've ever told me about a woman?

368
00:23:57,928 --> 00:23:58,928
I know.

369
00:24:00,938 --> 00:24:02,338
Thank you for telling me.

370
00:24:03,138 --> 00:24:04,438
I appreciate it, but...

371
00:24:11,248 --> 00:24:13,848
The reason I'm telling you this, Mother,

372
00:24:16,078 --> 00:24:17,618
is because I need your help.

373
00:24:18,688 --> 00:24:20,718
My help? What for?

374
00:24:21,888 --> 00:24:23,688
I need your help,

375
00:24:24,688 --> 00:24:25,988
so I don't give up on her.

376
00:24:29,398 --> 00:24:32,568
As long as you believe in me, then no matter what happens,

377
00:24:32,798 --> 00:24:34,338
I won't give up on her.

378
00:24:38,268 --> 00:24:39,268
Mu Jin.

379
00:24:39,338 --> 00:24:42,278
I'll report back if there's good news. Good night.

380
00:24:50,918 --> 00:24:52,418
Why, that kid...

381
00:24:54,458 --> 00:24:55,488
Honestly...

382
00:25:31,328 --> 00:25:33,328
You might think I'm a total loser,

383
00:25:33,498 --> 00:25:35,628
but I'm going to confess to you ten more times.

384
00:25:36,358 --> 00:25:37,828
Reject me nine times,

385
00:25:38,498 --> 00:25:39,938
but accept me just once.

386
00:25:47,738 --> 00:25:49,238
Sleep well, Gyu Rim.

387
00:25:49,808 --> 00:25:52,978
See you tomorrow. I'll be thrilled to see you.

388
00:26:18,908 --> 00:26:20,108
Because you're the eldest daughter.

389
00:26:20,978 --> 00:26:24,078
You're the nice one. You're always giving and selfless,

390
00:26:24,148 --> 00:26:25,448
and so compassionate, an eldest daughter trait.

391
00:26:30,848 --> 00:26:33,488
Like Gyu Min says, you're Kongjwi, and I'm Patjwi.

392
00:26:33,788 --> 00:26:35,858
We're just playing our parts.

393
00:26:36,488 --> 00:26:38,828
It's in your DNA. You were born that way.

394
00:27:05,748 --> 00:27:08,018
You scared me. Ever heard of knocking?

395
00:27:08,458 --> 00:27:10,158
Do you know how to use the washing machine?

396
00:27:10,188 --> 00:27:11,258
How about the blankets?

397
00:27:11,358 --> 00:27:13,158
Do you know how to make radish kimchi?

398
00:27:14,058 --> 00:27:15,398
What is she going on about?

399
00:27:16,628 --> 00:27:19,768
Gyu Oh is allergic to cucumbers, and Gyu Seo won't eat carrots.

400
00:27:19,838 --> 00:27:21,668
And Gyu Min needs you to read to her before bed.

401
00:27:21,738 --> 00:27:23,208
Listen here, Ms. Han Gyu Rim.

402
00:27:23,768 --> 00:27:26,008
Why are you suddenly telling me all this?

403
00:27:26,068 --> 00:27:27,538
Because you're doing it from now on.

404
00:27:27,608 --> 00:27:29,708
If you don't know how, look it up online and learn.

405
00:27:29,908 --> 00:27:32,908
Since you're so smart, you'll learn everything much faster than me.

406
00:27:33,448 --> 00:27:35,718
And what will you be doing? Are you going somewhere?

407
00:27:37,318 --> 00:27:38,688
I asked where you're going.

408
00:27:39,418 --> 00:27:41,558
- I am. - Where are you going?

409
00:27:41,988 --> 00:27:42,988
I'm...

410
00:27:43,958 --> 00:27:44,988
I'm getting married.

411
00:27:46,388 --> 00:27:47,398
What?

412
00:27:49,498 --> 00:27:53,338
- You're what? Getting married? - That's right.

413
00:27:54,068 --> 00:27:56,638
Come on, be serious. If you're going to lie,

414
00:27:56,638 --> 00:27:58,368
at least make it believable...

415
00:27:58,438 --> 00:27:59,508
so I can pretend to fall for it.

416
00:27:59,568 --> 00:28:01,438
You haven't had a real relationship since high school.

417
00:28:01,508 --> 00:28:02,638
I know everything.

418
00:28:02,638 --> 00:28:05,048
How on earth could you be getting married?

419
00:28:05,478 --> 00:28:06,918
Is getting married some kind of trick?

420
00:28:06,978 --> 00:28:08,118
You do it when you're in love.

421
00:28:08,178 --> 00:28:10,288
That's my point. When did you ever have time...

422
00:28:10,288 --> 00:28:11,688
to date and fall in love?

423
00:28:11,748 --> 00:28:13,088
It only takes ten seconds to fall for someone.

424
00:28:13,148 --> 00:28:14,488
I couldn't run around everywhere like you...

425
00:28:14,558 --> 00:28:16,188
dating whenever I felt like it.

426
00:28:16,188 --> 00:28:17,828
We worked together, went to work together,

427
00:28:17,888 --> 00:28:20,158
and came home together. We made it work. What about it?

428
00:28:22,298 --> 00:28:24,528
Okay. Fine. Let's just say that's true.

429
00:28:25,498 --> 00:28:27,738
Then show me the person you're going to marry.

430
00:28:28,038 --> 00:28:29,038
What?

431
00:28:29,398 --> 00:28:31,908
Why? You're my sister and you're getting married,

432
00:28:31,968 --> 00:28:33,908
so shouldn't I get to meet my future brother-in-law?

433
00:28:34,308 --> 00:28:36,608
Why? You'll see him at the wedding.

434
00:28:36,678 --> 00:28:38,508
Bring him to meet me before the end of the week.

435
00:28:39,008 --> 00:28:40,078
Then I'll believe you.

436
00:28:40,348 --> 00:28:41,918
He's a very busy person.

437
00:28:41,978 --> 00:28:45,388
Look at you. If you're going to lie, at least use your brain...

438
00:28:45,448 --> 00:28:48,118
and come up with something that's a little convincing.

439
00:28:53,658 --> 00:28:55,728
Of all your jokes, Han Gyu Rim, this one is the funniest.

440
00:28:57,428 --> 00:28:58,528
This Saturday.

441
00:29:00,198 --> 00:29:02,568
You can meet him this Saturday.

442
00:29:03,968 --> 00:29:06,338
Happy now? You'd better show up, or you're dead.

443
00:29:19,718 --> 00:29:21,558
I'm crazy. I'm insane.

444
00:29:22,318 --> 00:29:24,788
What have I done just to get one over on Han Gyu Young?

445
00:29:25,688 --> 00:29:27,058
What am I going to do?

446
00:29:28,858 --> 00:29:30,228
Oh, honestly.

447
00:29:37,238 --> 00:29:38,308
Hey, Han Gyu Oh.

448
00:29:39,138 --> 00:29:41,038
Did you know Han Gyu Rim is getting married?

449
00:29:41,978 --> 00:29:43,138
Hey, you twins.

450
00:29:44,478 --> 00:29:46,918
Your sister Gyu Rim is ditching you all to get married.

451
00:29:46,918 --> 00:29:48,378
What are you going to do now?

452
00:29:59,288 --> 00:30:00,358
Gyu Rim.

453
00:30:00,728 --> 00:30:01,828
Gyu Rim.

454
00:30:02,098 --> 00:30:04,428
Is what Gyu Young said true?

455
00:30:06,128 --> 00:30:08,068
No, it's just that...

456
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:10,068
Are you really getting married?

457
00:30:11,738 --> 00:30:15,238
They're about to cry. Just confess before they start crying.

458
00:30:17,578 --> 00:30:18,578
Right.

459
00:30:19,008 --> 00:30:20,348
Yesterday, when you said you had something to tell me

460
00:30:20,348 --> 00:30:21,848
so I should come home early,

461
00:30:21,918 --> 00:30:23,488
were you going to tell me you're getting married?

462
00:30:24,348 --> 00:30:26,618
No, it's not that, it's...

463
00:30:30,088 --> 00:30:31,088
Yes.

464
00:30:31,628 --> 00:30:32,628
All of a sudden?

465
00:30:33,558 --> 00:30:34,858
Without any warning?

466
00:30:36,498 --> 00:30:39,468
Who even gets married at 24 these days?

467
00:30:39,598 --> 00:30:42,468
Why? What? I can if I want to.

468
00:30:43,368 --> 00:30:45,268
Why are you all looking at me like that?

469
00:30:46,168 --> 00:30:47,978
To be blunt, I'm not your mother.

470
00:30:49,108 --> 00:30:50,678
Am I supposed to spend my whole life making your meals,

471
00:30:50,748 --> 00:30:52,278
doing your laundry, washing the dishes, and vacuuming,

472
00:30:52,348 --> 00:30:55,318
and then go out and work a part-time job?

473
00:30:55,448 --> 00:30:56,448
And never get married?

474
00:30:56,848 --> 00:30:58,988
No, that's not what I meant.

475
00:31:01,558 --> 00:31:05,058
- Don't go. Stay with us. - Don't go.

476
00:31:05,128 --> 00:31:08,728
- Don't go. - Don't worry.

477
00:31:08,798 --> 00:31:10,868
- Gyu Rim. - Even if I'm gone,

478
00:31:10,928 --> 00:31:11,928
Gyu Young will take care of you.

479
00:31:13,028 --> 00:31:15,068
- Gyu Rim, don't go. - Me?

480
00:31:17,268 --> 00:31:19,168
Gyu Rim...

481
00:31:19,168 --> 00:31:20,838
Don't go, Gyu Rim.

482
00:31:21,608 --> 00:31:23,478
Gyu Rim...

483
00:31:33,018 --> 00:31:34,318
What am I supposed to do?

484
00:31:38,158 --> 00:31:40,558
Gosh, Han Gyu Rim, you've got some nerve.

485
00:31:40,558 --> 00:31:41,628
You even made them cry.

486
00:31:41,728 --> 00:31:44,868
- What's that supposed to mean? - I thought you'd admit lying.

487
00:31:45,128 --> 00:31:46,568
I'm telling you, it's not a lie. It's real.

488
00:31:46,838 --> 00:31:48,898
Fine. We'll find out on Saturday.

489
00:31:49,268 --> 00:31:52,668
Gosh, I'm suddenly so excited for Saturday.

490
00:32:09,888 --> 00:32:11,688
I should've just said I was joining the army.

491
00:32:12,458 --> 00:32:14,258
This is why you're so stupid.

492
00:32:14,258 --> 00:32:15,798
It's why people always walk all over you.

493
00:32:16,228 --> 00:32:17,228
Darn.

494
00:32:18,568 --> 00:32:19,628
Why are you hitting your head?

495
00:32:34,818 --> 00:32:35,818
Well...

496
00:32:38,418 --> 00:32:39,788
About the text I sent last night...

497
00:32:42,758 --> 00:32:44,388
I had a bit to drink.

498
00:32:46,558 --> 00:32:48,758
It's okay. You don't have to apologise.

499
00:32:48,998 --> 00:32:50,468
I meant every word.

500
00:32:54,498 --> 00:32:57,068
If I came on too strong...

501
00:32:58,438 --> 00:32:59,568
and caught you off guard,

502
00:33:00,338 --> 00:33:01,538
from now on,

503
00:33:02,238 --> 00:33:03,508
I'll take things slower.

504
00:33:06,208 --> 00:33:07,548
So you won't feel overwhelmed.

505
00:33:08,448 --> 00:33:11,088
When I help you and look out for you,

506
00:33:11,848 --> 00:33:14,358
or even if I lose my cool and meddle in your business,

507
00:33:16,958 --> 00:33:18,628
just think of it as camaraderie,

508
00:33:20,558 --> 00:33:21,928
and don't feel pressured.

509
00:33:26,698 --> 00:33:27,898
In return, Gyu Rim,

510
00:33:29,738 --> 00:33:31,208
you just keep letting your heart flutter for me.

511
00:33:32,568 --> 00:33:33,678
You don't have to show it.

512
00:33:35,938 --> 00:33:37,108
But it'd be even better if you did.

513
00:33:47,858 --> 00:33:52,088
(City Bus Route Map)

514
00:34:01,368 --> 00:34:02,938
(Gyu Young)

515
00:34:07,908 --> 00:34:08,908
Yes?

516
00:34:09,838 --> 00:34:11,608
The man sitting next to you.

517
00:34:12,178 --> 00:34:13,618
Is he the one you're marrying?

518
00:34:21,018 --> 00:34:22,258
Yes.

519
00:34:22,788 --> 00:34:23,788
Liar.

520
00:34:37,138 --> 00:34:39,608
I'm not lying. I'm busy. Bye.

521
00:34:41,438 --> 00:34:42,438
Hey.

522
00:34:44,378 --> 00:34:45,378
Darn.

523
00:34:46,678 --> 00:34:48,778
Did you just brush some dust off my clothes?

524
00:34:50,848 --> 00:34:51,848
Yes.

525
00:35:08,468 --> 00:35:10,508
For real? Is your sister really getting married?

526
00:35:11,768 --> 00:35:13,468
Are you serious? You actually believe that?

527
00:35:14,308 --> 00:35:15,308
It's not true?

528
00:35:15,678 --> 00:35:18,148
How can you be a TA when you're so clueless?

529
00:35:19,578 --> 00:35:21,148
If someone tells you that you have a "pure soul..."

530
00:35:21,218 --> 00:35:22,518
or asks if you're "spiritually curious..."

531
00:35:22,578 --> 00:35:24,388
and tells you to follow them for some ritual,

532
00:35:24,818 --> 00:35:26,388
you run and don't ever look back.

533
00:35:27,758 --> 00:35:29,388
You should know better than to believe everything.

534
00:35:29,458 --> 00:35:32,128
Han Gyu Rim is having a hard time, putting on this ridiculous show...

535
00:35:35,498 --> 00:35:37,168
But then, who was that guy?

536
00:35:37,498 --> 00:35:40,668
- What guy? - He felt like a last-minute hire.

537
00:35:41,538 --> 00:35:44,368
But he was a total hottie, even from a distance.

538
00:35:44,738 --> 00:35:45,908
I'm telling you, it's true.

539
00:35:45,968 --> 00:35:48,778
My friend had lunch at that hotel and saw the whole thing.

540
00:35:49,178 --> 00:35:50,508
She saw Han Gyu Young try to pull a gold-digger scam...

541
00:35:50,578 --> 00:35:51,578
and get totally humiliated.

542
00:35:52,148 --> 00:35:55,448
I'm getting secondhand embarrassment just hearing about it.

543
00:35:55,818 --> 00:35:58,918
- Is she incapable of feeling shame? - Are you kidding? Of course not.

544
00:35:59,518 --> 00:36:01,788
Why else do you think her nickname is "The Draft Board?"

545
00:36:02,118 --> 00:36:03,788
They say a truckload of guys have joined the army,

546
00:36:03,858 --> 00:36:05,688
taken leaves of absence, or dropped out because of her.

547
00:36:06,158 --> 00:36:07,758
Seriously, can she not survive a single day...

548
00:36:07,828 --> 00:36:08,828
without a man?

549
00:36:09,658 --> 00:36:10,668
She's a disgrace to women,

550
00:36:10,728 --> 00:36:12,328
to the medical school, and to our university.

551
00:36:19,268 --> 00:36:20,608
Sorry.

552
00:36:21,008 --> 00:36:23,948
It smelled so foul, I thought this was a trash can.

553
00:36:24,248 --> 00:36:26,848
You little.... Hey, are you crazy?

554
00:36:27,948 --> 00:36:29,078
Hey, are you okay?

555
00:36:32,848 --> 00:36:37,088
- Hey. Hey, are you crazy? - Hyun Ju, are you okay?

556
00:36:38,728 --> 00:36:41,258
I know you've liked Shin Jeong Rok since you were a freshman.

557
00:36:41,598 --> 00:36:43,798
I know you confessed to him and got rejected.

558
00:36:44,168 --> 00:36:45,328
And I know you're super jealous...

559
00:36:45,398 --> 00:36:46,768
because you know he and I are dating.

560
00:36:47,938 --> 00:36:49,138
So know your place.

561
00:36:49,968 --> 00:36:51,408
Who can you blame for not being good enough?

562
00:36:51,838 --> 00:36:52,838
Are you okay?

563
00:36:53,708 --> 00:36:55,578
I won't stop you from being her willing lackeys,

564
00:36:56,038 --> 00:36:58,178
but it's pathetic to watch, so you guys should tone it down too.

565
00:37:03,378 --> 00:37:04,748
Has she lost her mind?

566
00:37:05,048 --> 00:37:07,158
- This is so annoying. - Are you okay?

567
00:37:14,528 --> 00:37:15,898
She's insane. Darn it.

568
00:37:23,568 --> 00:37:25,168
What should we do?

569
00:37:26,768 --> 00:37:27,778
Unbelievable.

570
00:37:30,748 --> 00:37:32,278
(My Wife)

571
00:37:33,108 --> 00:37:35,248
- Hey, honey. - Where are you?

572
00:37:35,848 --> 00:37:38,248
I'm at the university. I'm here to see President Kim.

573
00:37:38,588 --> 00:37:39,588
How about you?

574
00:37:39,648 --> 00:37:42,618
Seo Hyun is working late, so I'm bringing her a dinner I made.

575
00:37:42,688 --> 00:37:43,788
I see.

576
00:37:43,788 --> 00:37:45,828
You're going back to the office, right?

577
00:37:46,128 --> 00:37:48,028
Well, I'll see after I meet with President Kim.

578
00:37:50,158 --> 00:37:51,168
Hello?

579
00:37:51,698 --> 00:37:53,628
Honey.

580
00:37:54,598 --> 00:37:56,838
Honey? What's wrong?

581
00:37:57,408 --> 00:37:58,508
Did you just get into an accident?

582
00:37:58,938 --> 00:38:00,208
It's nothing.

583
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:03,078
- I was being a little careless. - You're not hurt, are you?

584
00:38:04,248 --> 00:38:05,248
Hello?

585
00:38:05,708 --> 00:38:07,478
It's okay. I'm not hurt.

586
00:38:08,318 --> 00:38:09,348
Where are you right now?

587
00:38:10,018 --> 00:38:12,718
- Honey. - This is driving me crazy.

588
00:38:12,788 --> 00:38:13,788
You're not hurt, right?

589
00:38:13,858 --> 00:38:15,218
- I'll call the insurance company... - What do you think you're doing?

590
00:38:15,218 --> 00:38:16,258
and take care of it.

591
00:38:16,318 --> 00:38:17,328
Don't worry too much.

592
00:38:17,388 --> 00:38:20,388
Seriously, who slams on their brakes at a yellow light?

593
00:38:20,628 --> 00:38:22,298
Roll down your window!

594
00:38:22,858 --> 00:38:23,928
Hello?

595
00:38:29,098 --> 00:38:30,098
- Honey? - Honey?

596
00:38:32,808 --> 00:38:33,838
Roll down your window.

597
00:38:34,608 --> 00:38:37,478
- I'll call you right back. - Okay, sure.

598
00:38:38,678 --> 00:38:39,678
Roll it down.

599
00:38:42,418 --> 00:38:44,648
It was just a minor fender bender.

600
00:38:46,188 --> 00:38:47,958
Yes, I called the insurance company right away.

601
00:38:50,658 --> 00:38:53,188
I told you I'm not hurt. I'm perfectly fine.

602
00:38:56,398 --> 00:38:57,398
Okay.

603
00:38:57,828 --> 00:39:00,498
I'll get a full checkup from head to toe...

604
00:39:01,238 --> 00:39:03,538
and show you that I'm completely fine.

605
00:39:03,798 --> 00:39:04,808
Will that make you happy?

606
00:39:06,138 --> 00:39:08,838
Yes. See you at home later, honey.

607
00:39:11,678 --> 00:39:13,708
Honey?

608
00:39:15,478 --> 00:39:16,878
You got remarried?

609
00:39:17,178 --> 00:39:19,518
Whether I get married again or a third time,

610
00:39:19,948 --> 00:39:21,488
what's it to you?

611
00:39:27,058 --> 00:39:29,328
- Why are you speaking like that? - Then,

612
00:39:30,028 --> 00:39:31,928
the wife who bore three children...

613
00:39:32,628 --> 00:39:35,698
to a scumbag like you who cheated and kicked me out overnight,

614
00:39:35,998 --> 00:39:37,438
has to speak to you with respect?

615
00:39:41,778 --> 00:39:44,178
Looks like you married well. From what I saw earlier,

616
00:39:45,378 --> 00:39:47,048
it looked like you were driving a nice car.

617
00:39:47,318 --> 00:39:48,318
Yes.

618
00:39:49,848 --> 00:39:51,218
As the kids say these days,

619
00:39:51,788 --> 00:39:54,218
out with the old junker and in with a luxury car.

620
00:39:54,918 --> 00:39:57,488
That saying is spot on. Are you doing well?

621
00:39:58,428 --> 00:40:00,958
Not that I'm actually curious, so you don't have to answer.

622
00:40:01,358 --> 00:40:04,998
Don't you miss the kids? You're living so well.

623
00:40:04,998 --> 00:40:06,528
How could you not have called even once?

624
00:40:06,828 --> 00:40:08,568
To our Gyu Rim, Gyu Oh, and Gyu Young.

625
00:40:09,468 --> 00:40:10,638
"I met your mother,"

626
00:40:11,238 --> 00:40:12,808
"and she's doing ridiculously well for herself."

627
00:40:13,068 --> 00:40:16,378
- What do you think they'd say? - And whose fault is all of that?

628
00:40:17,378 --> 00:40:19,008
You're the one who made everything this way.

629
00:40:19,378 --> 00:40:20,508
Well, in that case,

630
00:40:20,848 --> 00:40:22,118
was I supposed to abandon the woman I love?

631
00:40:22,718 --> 00:40:25,588
She said I was all she had. The woman carrying my child.

632
00:40:25,988 --> 00:40:26,988
Was I supposed to brand her as an adulteress?

633
00:40:29,688 --> 00:40:34,028
Right. What a tear-jerking romance.

634
00:40:34,798 --> 00:40:36,028
If only it weren't about me.

635
00:40:37,898 --> 00:40:38,898
Did you get work done on your face?

636
00:40:40,298 --> 00:40:41,538
You got younger and prettier...

637
00:40:42,968 --> 00:40:44,468
than when we broke up.

638
00:40:46,908 --> 00:40:48,078
Shut your mouth.

639
00:40:48,838 --> 00:40:51,578
Tell your wife this. If I hear she's mistreating my kids...

640
00:40:51,648 --> 00:40:52,808
even the slightest bit,

641
00:40:53,408 --> 00:40:55,218
I'll come over and kill her myself.

642
00:40:59,618 --> 00:41:00,618
She's gone.

643
00:41:01,518 --> 00:41:03,718
She ran off a long time ago. She left the twins.

644
00:41:04,858 --> 00:41:06,928
Why?

645
00:41:07,928 --> 00:41:09,198
Did you cheat on her too?

646
00:41:09,628 --> 00:41:11,928
I didn't cheat. She did.

647
00:41:12,728 --> 00:41:15,268
You know that jerk, the head of accounting?

648
00:41:15,338 --> 00:41:16,338
The lanky one.

649
00:41:16,398 --> 00:41:19,068
The one who was totally bald. It was him.

650
00:41:19,808 --> 00:41:20,808
What about the kids?

651
00:41:22,008 --> 00:41:23,008
The kids...

652
00:41:23,378 --> 00:41:25,908
How long have they been living without a mother?

653
00:41:27,278 --> 00:41:30,148
A while now. About six years?

654
00:41:31,688 --> 00:41:34,518
That's why I'm trying to find a mother for my poor kids.

655
00:41:34,818 --> 00:41:36,418
I'm still looking hard.

656
00:41:39,128 --> 00:41:42,358
But no matter how hard I look, no one's as good as their real mom.

657
00:41:43,458 --> 00:41:45,328
Hey, instead of this,

658
00:41:46,068 --> 00:41:47,368
why don't you go see the kids?

659
00:41:51,068 --> 00:41:52,808
Come on. Let's go.

660
00:41:52,868 --> 00:41:54,138
We'll get this to go.

661
00:41:54,438 --> 00:41:57,238
If you see the children you gave birth to,

662
00:41:57,238 --> 00:41:58,778
you might have a change of heart.

663
00:41:59,578 --> 00:42:00,818
Get out of my way now.

664
00:42:01,578 --> 00:42:04,418
And from now on, if you see me, don't you dare act like you know me.

665
00:42:04,948 --> 00:42:07,988
I was wrong, honey. Okay? Honey.

666
00:42:09,088 --> 00:42:12,628
I've realised after all this time that there's no one like you.

667
00:42:13,258 --> 00:42:15,258
I'm paying for my sins.

668
00:42:16,128 --> 00:42:18,228
I'm so sorry, honey. I'm truly sorry.

669
00:42:19,298 --> 00:42:23,098
No. Hey, please come back. You're Gyu Rim's mother, aren't you?

670
00:42:23,868 --> 00:42:25,968
For our poor kids' sake, please.

671
00:42:26,108 --> 00:42:27,938
Even if you hate me, give me one more chance.

672
00:42:28,678 --> 00:42:31,678
- Honey, please, one more chance... - Let go of me, you jerk.

673
00:42:45,928 --> 00:42:47,798
What's wrong? Are you sick?

674
00:42:48,258 --> 00:42:50,698
I think the tofu I had for lunch was bad.

675
00:42:51,298 --> 00:42:55,498
My stomach's rumbling again. And there's nothing left in there.

676
00:42:57,738 --> 00:43:00,638
Hey, are you like this in front of Mu Jin too?

677
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:04,378
Do you tell Mu Jin everything about your body with no filter?

678
00:43:04,448 --> 00:43:06,478
Are you crazy? When I'm married to Mu Jin,

679
00:43:06,478 --> 00:43:09,478
- I'm not even going to fart. - Marriage? Sure.

680
00:43:09,718 --> 00:43:11,448
He's ignoring your texts and your emails.

681
00:43:11,948 --> 00:43:13,688
Didn't you get brutally rejected by Mu Jin?

682
00:43:13,688 --> 00:43:16,058
I haven't been officially rejected yet.

683
00:43:19,188 --> 00:43:22,058
Right, it's too soon to give up hope.

684
00:43:23,058 --> 00:43:24,168
Speaking of which, Seo Hyun.

685
00:43:25,068 --> 00:43:26,068
Let's form an alliance.

686
00:43:26,428 --> 00:43:27,428
An alliance?

687
00:43:28,098 --> 00:43:29,098
What kind of alliance?

688
00:43:29,168 --> 00:43:32,008
I'm not quite sure how to explain this,

689
00:43:32,508 --> 00:43:35,038
but you, me, Mu Jin, and Han Gyu Rim...

690
00:43:35,138 --> 00:43:37,948
Our relationships are all tangled up in a complicated way.

691
00:43:38,208 --> 00:43:39,208
Han Gyu Rim?

692
00:43:39,708 --> 00:43:40,708
Who is Han Gyu Rim?

693
00:43:42,978 --> 00:43:44,988
Han Gyu Rim is the one Mu Jin likes, isn't she?

694
00:43:45,148 --> 00:43:48,518
When it comes to Mu Jin, you're a psychic.

695
00:43:48,558 --> 00:43:51,428
It's like you're possessed. Anyway, the important thing is...

696
00:43:53,728 --> 00:43:55,128
I like Han Gyu Rim too.

697
00:43:57,928 --> 00:43:59,068
What's so special about Han Gyu Rim?

698
00:43:59,668 --> 00:44:00,898
Is she really all that?

699
00:44:01,468 --> 00:44:05,438
Well, it's not that she's amazing, but her charm is irresistible.

700
00:44:05,668 --> 00:44:08,278
She's kind, cute, and pretty all at once. Can you believe it?

701
00:44:08,338 --> 00:44:11,108
Anyway, this is my first time being rivals with Mu Jin...

702
00:44:11,178 --> 00:44:13,108
over a girl.

703
00:44:13,448 --> 00:44:17,548
You like Mu Jin, and I like Han Gyu Rim.

704
00:44:17,848 --> 00:44:19,248
If things work out between you and Mu Jin,

705
00:44:19,518 --> 00:44:21,288
my chances of getting with Han Gyu Rim will also go up.

706
00:44:22,188 --> 00:44:23,788
So, an alliance?

707
00:44:24,688 --> 00:44:28,298
I'll do my absolute best to help you and Mu Jin get together.

708
00:44:29,058 --> 00:44:31,768
So in return, you need to use all of your expertise...

709
00:44:31,828 --> 00:44:33,798
and turn me into the most charming man alive.

710
00:44:33,928 --> 00:44:35,738
So Han Gyu Rim will fall head over heels for me.

711
00:44:35,798 --> 00:44:37,538
Just what kind of girl is this Han Gyu Rim?

712
00:44:38,108 --> 00:44:40,368
What's so great about her that both Kim Mu Jin and Park Jung Woo...

713
00:44:40,438 --> 00:44:42,438
are falling all over yourselves for her?

714
00:45:12,838 --> 00:45:14,838
Han Gyu Oh is totally ruined.

715
00:45:15,438 --> 00:45:17,578
So he can't come to school for ten days?

716
00:45:17,908 --> 00:45:19,108
Because of the suspension, he probably...

717
00:45:19,178 --> 00:45:20,278
can't enter the competition either.

718
00:45:20,578 --> 00:45:22,078
Doesn't that mean he won't get into a sports university?

719
00:45:22,948 --> 00:45:24,718
What's he going to do?

720
00:45:26,348 --> 00:45:27,348
Hey.

721
00:46:16,098 --> 00:46:17,568
Jerk.

722
00:46:18,568 --> 00:46:21,538
How can love just change?

723
00:46:24,108 --> 00:46:25,108
Excuse me.

724
00:46:27,648 --> 00:46:28,778
Can you go cry somewhere else?

725
00:46:31,418 --> 00:46:33,688
Hey, do you own this place or something?

726
00:46:34,488 --> 00:46:35,558
This is where I and...

727
00:46:38,628 --> 00:46:41,328
Oh, no! I dropped my phone!

728
00:46:41,558 --> 00:46:43,798
My phone! What am I going to do?

729
00:46:43,858 --> 00:46:47,398
- Oh, no! - It's dangerous. Are you crazy?

730
00:46:47,468 --> 00:46:50,838
What if he calls me? My phone.

731
00:46:51,808 --> 00:46:53,208
I'll get it for you,

732
00:46:53,738 --> 00:46:55,438
so don't do anything foolish and stay put.

733
00:46:57,138 --> 00:46:59,608
- My phone. - Answer me.

734
00:47:02,048 --> 00:47:03,048
Okay.

735
00:47:12,988 --> 00:47:13,988
Almost there.

736
00:47:24,538 --> 00:47:26,738
Why is it on?

737
00:47:26,808 --> 00:47:30,178
How is it in perfect condition?

738
00:47:34,678 --> 00:47:35,678
Hey.

739
00:47:38,488 --> 00:47:40,248
This...

740
00:47:40,618 --> 00:47:43,188
For just a few hours...

741
00:47:43,988 --> 00:47:48,158
No, even one hour is fine. Can you hold on to this for me?

742
00:47:48,628 --> 00:47:49,658
Why should I?

743
00:47:50,328 --> 00:47:51,498
Because I'm afraid I won't be able to...

744
00:47:51,568 --> 00:47:52,728
stop myself from calling that jerk.

745
00:47:53,598 --> 00:47:57,298
I'll end up crying and begging him and making a total scene.

746
00:47:58,438 --> 00:47:59,438
A hundred dollars.

747
00:48:02,978 --> 00:48:04,978
I'll pay you 100 dollars an hour.

748
00:48:05,278 --> 00:48:07,308
It'll be 100 dollars an hour...

749
00:48:07,678 --> 00:48:09,218
and 200 dollars for 2 hours.

750
00:48:09,778 --> 00:48:10,778
No.

751
00:48:11,048 --> 00:48:14,388
Considering all the trouble I'm going to cause you in that time,

752
00:48:14,888 --> 00:48:16,758
I'll give you 300 dollars.

753
00:48:18,588 --> 00:48:20,328
Considering what part-time jobs pay these days,

754
00:48:20,688 --> 00:48:22,598
this is an incredibly high-paying gig.

755
00:48:24,228 --> 00:48:25,228
Deal.

756
00:48:27,298 --> 00:48:28,898
But don't try to back out later.

757
00:48:30,468 --> 00:48:31,468
Got it.

758
00:48:32,268 --> 00:48:33,268
Thank you.

759
00:48:47,448 --> 00:48:48,458
Welcome.

760
00:48:52,488 --> 00:48:53,788
Please have a seat wherever you'd like.

761
00:48:53,858 --> 00:48:55,928
- Would you like to sit here? - Yes.

762
00:49:02,468 --> 00:49:04,368
Hello. Here's your menu.

763
00:49:04,438 --> 00:49:06,208
Please take your time and order when you're ready.

764
00:49:06,268 --> 00:49:07,508
I'll be right back with some water.

765
00:49:10,708 --> 00:49:13,178
Are you waiting for someone?

766
00:49:13,648 --> 00:49:15,618
Oh, Gyu Rim...

767
00:49:16,018 --> 00:49:18,318
I'm looking for Han Gyu Rim.

768
00:49:18,648 --> 00:49:20,018
Han Gyu Rim? Why?

769
00:49:20,318 --> 00:49:24,258
Oh, that's none of your business. Just get that young woman for me.

770
00:49:25,458 --> 00:49:28,158
Gyu Rim stepped out for a moment.

771
00:49:28,428 --> 00:49:30,428
Oh, dear, then when will she be back?

772
00:49:31,228 --> 00:49:34,028
I really have to see that young woman today.

773
00:49:34,568 --> 00:49:38,468
- I have to meet and repay kindness. - Her kindness?

774
00:49:41,508 --> 00:49:43,008
Driver, please open the door.

775
00:49:48,148 --> 00:49:50,318
Ma'am, are you okay?

776
00:49:50,848 --> 00:49:51,848
Ma'am.

777
00:49:52,348 --> 00:49:53,448
By any chance,

778
00:49:53,848 --> 00:49:56,688
are you the elderly woman Gyu Rim helped a little while ago?

779
00:49:56,818 --> 00:49:58,728
- At the bus stop. - That's right.

780
00:49:59,058 --> 00:50:01,658
So that Gyu Rim girl must have told you.

781
00:50:01,758 --> 00:50:05,668
No, I was there with her that day. You may not remember, though.

782
00:50:06,898 --> 00:50:10,638
- You were there that day too? - Yes, well...

783
00:50:10,998 --> 00:50:13,408
Gyu Rim and I were on the bus, and it was just about to leave...

784
00:50:13,468 --> 00:50:14,908
when you collapsed.

785
00:50:15,938 --> 00:50:18,178
What? So...

786
00:50:19,008 --> 00:50:23,348
you're telling me you saw someone collapse and just left?

787
00:50:23,418 --> 00:50:26,548
- It wasn't me. The bus took off... - Never mind.

788
00:50:26,918 --> 00:50:30,418
Oh, there's no point in blaming or resenting you now.

789
00:50:30,488 --> 00:50:32,058
What's that going to change?

790
00:50:32,958 --> 00:50:35,458
These days, you're hardly the only one...

791
00:50:35,528 --> 00:50:37,298
who's worse than an animal.

792
00:50:38,768 --> 00:50:40,098
Come to think of it,

793
00:50:40,768 --> 00:50:43,898
someone like that Gyu Rim girl is a rare breed.

794
00:50:44,168 --> 00:50:46,238
A true national treasure.

795
00:50:47,238 --> 00:50:51,808
You worthless bum. You heartless man.

796
00:50:52,808 --> 00:50:53,808
Unbelievable.

797
00:50:55,278 --> 00:50:56,978
I'll be right back with your water.

798
00:51:04,728 --> 00:51:06,758
Is she brave or just stupid?

799
00:51:23,108 --> 00:51:24,338
Seriously.

800
00:51:24,648 --> 00:51:26,208
I want to get a drink.

801
00:51:28,848 --> 00:51:31,148
- Hey, is that Yeon Soo? - What do I do?

802
00:51:31,648 --> 00:51:32,748
What should I do?

803
00:51:34,418 --> 00:51:37,688
Okay. Then get me a cold one.

804
00:51:37,918 --> 00:51:39,488
- Okay, I'll go buy one. - Okay.

805
00:51:51,238 --> 00:51:52,238
I...

806
00:51:53,208 --> 00:51:54,408
I thought you were someone I knew.

807
00:51:54,778 --> 00:51:55,778
Shoot.

808
00:52:05,918 --> 00:52:07,248
You don't want to run into him, right?

809
00:52:09,888 --> 00:52:12,088
On the count of three, we're getting up.

810
00:52:12,088 --> 00:52:15,558
Just look straight ahead and walk. One, two,

811
00:52:15,828 --> 00:52:16,898
three.

812
00:52:46,328 --> 00:52:47,428
Thank you...

813
00:52:48,058 --> 00:52:49,828
for everything you did for me today.

814
00:52:50,228 --> 00:52:51,228
Well...

815
00:52:51,768 --> 00:52:54,028
Sure. Take care.

816
00:53:00,438 --> 00:53:01,438
Shoot.

817
00:53:03,938 --> 00:53:04,948
Right, 100 dollars.

818
00:53:06,508 --> 00:53:07,508
Excuse me!

819
00:53:08,178 --> 00:53:09,178
Hey!

820
00:53:10,748 --> 00:53:12,118
Hey, your pay!

821
00:53:23,998 --> 00:53:27,468
- Nice to see you again. - I'm not here to see you today.

822
00:53:27,498 --> 00:53:30,138
- I'm here to get my mom. - Get your mom?

823
00:53:42,848 --> 00:53:45,548
- How did you know I was here? - Mom, let's go.

824
00:53:46,318 --> 00:53:49,358
- Hey, just go on in. - Let's just go.

825
00:53:49,358 --> 00:53:51,588
- Hey, wait a minute. - Let's go, Mom.

826
00:53:51,628 --> 00:53:52,788
I told you, I have to see Gyu Rim.

827
00:53:53,358 --> 00:53:58,128
- Hello, ma'am. - Oh, my. Are you just arriving?

828
00:53:58,668 --> 00:54:01,438
It's really good to see you again.

829
00:54:01,938 --> 00:54:05,108
It makes me so happy to see you looking so healthy.

830
00:54:05,708 --> 00:54:09,208
My son said he wanted to thank you with a reward,

831
00:54:09,338 --> 00:54:13,048
or at least buy you a meal. He was so insistent,

832
00:54:13,308 --> 00:54:15,748
so why didn't you let him do anything?

833
00:54:16,548 --> 00:54:19,988
I feel I absolutely must repay your kindness.

834
00:54:20,348 --> 00:54:21,658
I'm really all right.

835
00:54:21,718 --> 00:54:24,488
Seeing you healthy is more than enough for me.

836
00:54:24,558 --> 00:54:26,788
Oh, my goodness.

837
00:54:27,358 --> 00:54:29,898
You even speak so beautifully.

838
00:54:30,198 --> 00:54:33,228
How could I not be charmed by you?

839
00:54:33,298 --> 00:54:37,598
All right, that's enough. You're making her uncomfortable.

840
00:54:38,268 --> 00:54:42,278
You know, my son was seeing a woman for over five years.

841
00:54:42,308 --> 00:54:44,138
Mom. Why are you talking about that?

842
00:54:44,138 --> 00:54:45,278
Just wait.

843
00:54:45,348 --> 00:54:47,878
We really adored her,

844
00:54:49,118 --> 00:54:51,648
but when our circumstances got a little difficult,

845
00:54:51,748 --> 00:54:55,018
she immediately showed her true colours.

846
00:54:55,788 --> 00:54:58,458
It turns out, if someone has no money, no connections,

847
00:54:58,528 --> 00:55:00,258
and nothing she can get out of them,

848
00:55:00,728 --> 00:55:04,158
she doesn't even treat them like a person. What a vile woman!

849
00:55:06,728 --> 00:55:09,968
- That's the kind of woman she was. - Mom. I told you to stop.

850
00:55:10,238 --> 00:55:11,738
- Let's go. - That incident... Oh, hey.

851
00:55:11,808 --> 00:55:14,268
- Come on, let's go. - Oh, honestly. Wait, you brat.

852
00:55:14,268 --> 00:55:15,808
After going through that,

853
00:55:16,138 --> 00:55:21,048
my health really suffered. I would just collapse all the time.

854
00:55:21,918 --> 00:55:26,748
But seeing a kind and lovely person like you,

855
00:55:27,148 --> 00:55:29,058
I feel so much better.

856
00:55:29,388 --> 00:55:30,588
My goodness.

857
00:55:33,058 --> 00:55:34,688
- Let's go. - Right.

858
00:55:35,328 --> 00:55:36,598
So what I'm saying is,

859
00:55:36,998 --> 00:55:41,498
consider it granting an old woman a wish,

860
00:55:42,468 --> 00:55:46,438
and meet my son just once... No, for just 15 minutes.

861
00:55:46,768 --> 00:55:48,108
Please meet with him.

862
00:55:48,638 --> 00:55:51,608
I mean, I'm not saying you have to do anything.

863
00:55:52,078 --> 00:55:56,948
Just meet him like a friend, have a meal, go on a date.

864
00:55:57,018 --> 00:55:58,688
But that sounds like you are asking her to do something.

865
00:55:59,248 --> 00:56:00,318
Excuse me?

866
00:56:00,848 --> 00:56:04,388
I'm not sure how repaying a kindness turned into granting your wish.

867
00:56:04,458 --> 00:56:07,428
According to you, Gyu Rim is your benefactor,

868
00:56:07,658 --> 00:56:10,758
so I don't understand why she also has to grant your wishes.

869
00:56:11,328 --> 00:56:14,028
Was I talking to you?

870
00:56:16,168 --> 00:56:17,698
No matter how I think about it,

871
00:56:17,998 --> 00:56:20,038
if I let a young woman like you get away,

872
00:56:20,038 --> 00:56:21,638
I feel like I'll regret it for the rest of my life.

873
00:56:22,138 --> 00:56:25,808
Where else would he find someone like you, Gyu Rim?

874
00:56:26,248 --> 00:56:28,348
- What do you say? - If you regret it, you regret it.

875
00:56:28,418 --> 00:56:29,818
If he can't find someone, then he can't find someone.

876
00:56:29,918 --> 00:56:31,848
Why do you keep putting pressure on Gyu Rim?

877
00:56:31,988 --> 00:56:33,548
Hey, you, stay out of this.

878
00:56:36,488 --> 00:56:38,158
Mu Jin, please go about your business.

879
00:56:38,888 --> 00:56:41,058
That's right. Mu Jin, you should go to another table.

880
00:56:49,568 --> 00:56:50,938
And you, young lady,

881
00:56:50,968 --> 00:56:54,608
don't hang around with a pretty boy like him.

882
00:56:54,978 --> 00:56:56,208
Don't even get close.

883
00:56:57,038 --> 00:57:00,378
He saw someone collapse and just walked away...

884
00:57:00,378 --> 00:57:01,778
because he was busy.

885
00:57:01,778 --> 00:57:05,948
- That's him. That wicked man. - Darn. Really?

886
00:57:06,788 --> 00:57:07,788
That little...

887
00:57:10,618 --> 00:57:11,888
- Let's go. - How could...

888
00:57:11,958 --> 00:57:13,388
- Are you out of your mind today? - Hey!

889
00:57:13,388 --> 00:57:14,528
- Just wait. - Let's go.

890
00:57:14,528 --> 00:57:15,628
- I said, wait. - Come on, let's go.

891
00:57:15,628 --> 00:57:17,128
Hey. You little brat.

892
00:57:21,598 --> 00:57:22,698
Are you disappointed in me?

893
00:57:23,268 --> 00:57:24,268
No.

894
00:57:25,868 --> 00:57:29,438
"Meet him and I'll buy you a meal. Meet him and go on a few dates."

895
00:57:30,578 --> 00:57:31,848
Not listening to the other person,

896
00:57:31,908 --> 00:57:34,148
just unilaterally pushing her own feelings and point of view.

897
00:57:34,448 --> 00:57:35,878
That's a form of violence too.

898
00:57:39,518 --> 00:57:40,548
Why are you looking at me like that?

899
00:57:40,548 --> 00:57:42,788
I'm just surprised to hear you, of all people,

900
00:57:42,788 --> 00:57:44,358
say something like that.

901
00:57:49,228 --> 00:57:50,228
So,

902
00:57:51,598 --> 00:57:52,798
are you really going to meet him?

903
00:57:53,968 --> 00:57:55,398
Are you that much of a pushover?

904
00:57:55,698 --> 00:57:56,968
You never listen to a single thing I say.

905
00:57:57,038 --> 00:57:59,038
When have I ever just done whatever they say?

906
00:57:59,138 --> 00:58:01,978
But you're going to do it, aren't you? Because she insisted.

907
00:58:02,038 --> 00:58:03,438
You'll give in because you're too soft-hearted.

908
00:58:05,048 --> 00:58:06,548
So that guy...

909
00:58:07,678 --> 00:58:10,118
Are you going to meet that old guy for a meal and go on a date?

910
00:58:10,518 --> 00:58:12,918
He's not old enough for you to be calling him that.

911
00:58:12,948 --> 00:58:14,718
Is that what's important right now?

912
00:58:15,858 --> 00:58:17,188
That old man... That guy...

913
00:58:18,018 --> 00:58:19,388
Are you really going to meet him?

914
00:58:20,628 --> 00:58:21,628
No.

915
00:58:39,248 --> 00:58:40,248
Hello?

916
00:58:40,608 --> 00:58:42,348
Am I speaking with Han Gyu Rim?

917
00:58:42,918 --> 00:58:43,978
Yes, this is she.

918
00:58:44,548 --> 00:58:47,548
Hi. I'm calling from the delivery department at Buy Mart.

919
00:58:48,018 --> 00:58:50,988
Han Gyu Young sent you a washing machine as a gift.

920
00:58:51,058 --> 00:58:52,988
When would be a good time for us to deliver it?

921
00:58:53,458 --> 00:58:56,628
Han Gyu Young sent what? A washing machine?

922
00:59:08,778 --> 00:59:09,908
Why are you here?

923
00:59:12,178 --> 00:59:13,408
I heard you refused the washing machine.

924
00:59:14,108 --> 00:59:15,748
Why a washing machine out of the blue?

925
00:59:16,648 --> 00:59:18,748
You put on that ridiculous act about getting married...

926
00:59:18,818 --> 00:59:20,048
because of the washing machine.

927
00:59:20,588 --> 00:59:22,658
I thought, "Han Gyu Rim, why is she suddenly acting so weird?

928
00:59:22,718 --> 00:59:24,218
I tried to figure out what the problem could be,

929
00:59:24,588 --> 00:59:26,388
and I realised the washing machine is ancient.

930
00:59:26,928 --> 00:59:28,388
So, with no money, I got you a special gift...

931
00:59:28,498 --> 00:59:29,758
A washing machine is a gift?

932
00:59:30,628 --> 00:59:32,168
So you're giving me better equipment

933
00:59:32,228 --> 00:59:33,768
just so I can keep doing the laundry?

934
00:59:33,898 --> 00:59:36,868
- No, that's not what I meant. - Han Gyu Young.

935
00:59:37,638 --> 00:59:39,768
What do you really take me for?

936
00:59:40,508 --> 00:59:42,538
It's not the washing machine? Then what is it?

937
00:59:42,838 --> 00:59:44,638
- A vacuum machine or a dishwasher? - Hey.

938
00:59:44,638 --> 00:59:46,048
Then what is it?

939
00:59:46,108 --> 00:59:48,878
Why do you suddenly want to get married?

940
00:59:49,378 --> 00:59:50,378
If you get married,

941
00:59:50,448 --> 00:59:51,918
what's supposed to happen to the rest of us?

942
00:59:51,988 --> 00:59:53,318
Are we all just supposed to die?

943
00:59:55,918 --> 00:59:58,088
Go. We can talk about this at home.

944
00:59:59,588 --> 01:00:01,458
I can't study because of you.

945
01:00:02,198 --> 01:00:04,098
The kids are still a crying mess over it.

946
01:00:04,228 --> 01:00:08,768
How are you going to fix this? It's a lie, right? It has to be.

947
01:00:09,598 --> 01:00:12,438
You're right. It was a lie.

948
01:00:13,368 --> 01:00:15,208
Like you said, I'm so busy trying to make ends meet,

949
01:00:15,278 --> 01:00:16,378
so 24 hours in a day isn't enough.

950
01:00:17,708 --> 01:00:21,208
How could I possibly have time to date? And even if I did,

951
01:00:22,518 --> 01:00:25,748
- who would marry someone like me? - Are you crazy?

952
01:00:25,748 --> 01:00:27,688
How could you lie about something like that?

953
01:00:28,518 --> 01:00:29,918
Because I was so exhausted,

954
01:00:31,488 --> 01:00:33,228
so sick and tired of everything,

955
01:00:33,588 --> 01:00:35,698
I just wanted to run away from it all. Is that so wrong?

956
01:00:36,098 --> 01:00:39,428
You're living just fine in your 1,500-dollar blouses,

957
01:00:39,568 --> 01:00:42,398
so why am I the only one stuck here suffering like this?

958
01:00:42,398 --> 01:00:44,538
I just wondered how long I have to keep living like this,

959
01:00:44,738 --> 01:00:46,808
and I was so frustrated I thought I'd go crazy.

960
01:00:46,868 --> 01:00:48,438
That's just your lot in life.

961
01:00:48,678 --> 01:00:50,538
What can you do? You were born that way.

962
01:00:52,948 --> 01:00:54,878
Is that any way to talk to your sister?

963
01:00:56,018 --> 01:00:57,248
You have no respect.

964
01:00:58,748 --> 01:01:01,348
Are you talking to me right now? And so informally?

965
01:01:04,618 --> 01:01:05,628
Wait.

966
01:01:06,888 --> 01:01:08,288
The bus stop?

967
01:01:08,698 --> 01:01:10,898
- Gyu Young. - Have a problem? Speak informally.

968
01:01:11,628 --> 01:01:14,128
- Who do you think you are? - I'm the man marrying your sister.

969
01:01:17,668 --> 01:01:20,338
What? You said it was a lie. You said it was all a lie.

970
01:01:20,338 --> 01:01:22,108
Your sister might be lying,

971
01:01:22,708 --> 01:01:25,078
but I'm serious. What are you going to do about it?

972
01:01:29,318 --> 01:01:30,878
Please, just stop.

973
01:01:32,888 --> 01:01:34,588
My family is poor,

974
01:01:35,388 --> 01:01:37,018
I have no savings,

975
01:01:37,718 --> 01:01:39,688
I have four younger siblings to support,

976
01:01:40,328 --> 01:01:41,688
and I didn't go to college.

977
01:01:42,828 --> 01:01:44,058
I don't have a mother.

978
01:01:45,498 --> 01:01:47,868
My father only comes home once every few months.

979
01:01:49,038 --> 01:01:51,338
So all my siblings depend on me.

980
01:01:53,668 --> 01:01:55,068
Getting involved with me means...

981
01:01:55,938 --> 01:01:59,208
playing the worst card in your hand, Mu Jin.

982
01:02:00,008 --> 01:02:01,408
If I wanted to be cruel,

983
01:02:01,408 --> 01:02:03,248
I could latch onto you and never let go.

984
01:02:04,978 --> 01:02:07,348
So unless you want to get dragged down...

985
01:02:07,418 --> 01:02:08,818
into this mess with me,

986
01:02:09,318 --> 01:02:11,588
you should count your blessings and run away while you can.

987
01:02:11,988 --> 01:02:12,988
No.

988
01:02:14,358 --> 01:02:15,558
I'm not running away.

989
01:02:20,068 --> 01:02:21,498
Whether it's a mess or not,

990
01:02:23,068 --> 01:02:25,438
I'll go anywhere as long as I'm with you, Gyu Rim.

991
01:02:27,008 --> 01:02:28,468
So don't you run away either.

992
01:02:32,308 --> 01:02:34,408
Well, look at you two. Quite the dramatic scene.

993
01:02:36,578 --> 01:02:37,618
If you've heard what you came to hear,

994
01:02:37,678 --> 01:02:38,688
would you mind leaving?

995
01:02:39,888 --> 01:02:41,848
And if I leave, what are you two going to do?

996
01:02:41,988 --> 01:02:44,618
What do you think a couple in love does?

997
01:02:46,028 --> 01:02:48,058
But hey, if you're into watching people,

998
01:02:48,128 --> 01:02:49,458
feel free to stay.

999
01:03:03,238 --> 01:03:04,538
Gyu Rim, could I...

1000
01:03:08,448 --> 01:03:09,878
hug you?

1001
01:03:12,688 --> 01:03:13,888
It's okay to say no.

1002
01:04:13,478 --> 01:04:16,918
(Love on the Menu)

1003
01:04:16,978 --> 01:04:18,788
He's Gyu Rim's boyfriend.

1004
01:04:18,848 --> 01:04:22,888
So you're dating, Gyu Rim? Looks like you landed a real catch.

1005
01:04:22,918 --> 01:04:24,318
Did you lie and say you were poor?

1006
01:04:24,758 --> 01:04:25,758
They're knockoffs.

1007
01:04:25,828 --> 01:04:27,528
Who are you trying to kid?

1008
01:04:27,528 --> 01:04:29,658
You're the spitting image of me when I was your age.

1009
01:04:29,698 --> 01:04:32,398
Mu Jin is different. He's not a liar.

1010
01:04:32,528 --> 01:04:34,428
I was worried Gyu Rim would get scared...

1011
01:04:34,498 --> 01:04:36,068
and run off. If I lose her now...

1012
01:04:36,068 --> 01:04:38,038
- I'm sorry. - I'll regret it for a lifetime.

1013
01:04:38,098 --> 01:04:40,608
You can either give up everything you have thanks to me,

1014
01:04:40,638 --> 01:04:43,408
- or you can get rid of that girl. - Han Gyu Rim.

1015
01:04:43,878 --> 01:04:46,608
I love you, Mu Jin.

